   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Three expected outputs are: (i) increased availability of food to vulnerable households; (ii) support the input needs of smallholders and marginal farmers; and (iii) an operational national food security response system. 
Indicator: 113,000 households reached through food distribution and food-for-work/cash-for-work program 
Progress/Status: A total of 224,810 households reached (198.95%).

Households reached directly through following activities:
a) Free rice distribution: 68,000 hhs; b) CFW: 38,931 hhs (8,937 female headed hhs); c) FFW: 19,667 hhs (6,453 female headed hhs); d) Civil works: 22,255 hhs (3,328 female headed hhs); e) ECLC: 127 (127 female headed hhs); f) School Feeding: 65,387 (31,555 girls); h) School Scholarship: 10,443 (5510 girls).
 Households reached indirectly through i) seed and fertilizer distribution: 73,625. 
Data Source: Quarterly Progress reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
