    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Three expected outputs are: (i) increased availability of food to vulnerable households; (ii) support the input needs of smallholders and marginal farmers; and (iii) an operational national food security response system. 
Indicator: Majority of beneficiaries reduced Rice consumption shortage by 3-4 months 
Progress/Status: Rice consumption needs of target beneficiaries for 3-4 months are met through series of short and medium term interventions. 

Rice consumption needs are met through a) free rice distribution equivalent of 3 months rice need per family; b) yield increase which reported to reduce food shortage of 1-3 months for most of the beneficiaries; c) CFW  which helped 38,931 beneficiary hhs earn $110 per hh; d) FFW  which provided 3,306 tons of rice to 19,667 beneficiary hhs. 
Data Source: Quarterly Progress reports 
